{\f1\fs24
SimpliSafe only sells their entry sensors in white, which looks out of place on dark window and door frames. These covers slide over both pieces of the 2-part entry sensor \emdash  the active side (with the status LED and reset button) and the passive magnetic side \emdash  letting you print them in any color or filament finish you like.\par
\par
Designed for a snug but removable fit: the covers slip on by hand, stay put during normal use, and come off cleanly if you ever need to access the sensor. A pill-shaped hole on the active-side cover lines up with the status LED. No hole is included for the reset button \emdash  the fit is snug enough that pressing through the wall isn\rquote t practical anyway. Just pull the cover off to reset and slide it back on; no adhesive needed.\par
\par
{\b Print Settings}\par
\par
{\b Material:} PLA or PETG (PETG recommended for longevity near windows in direct sun)\par
{\b Layer height:} 0.2 mm\par
{\b Perimeters / walls:} 2 (0.8 mm at 0.4 mm nozzle)\par
{\b Supports:} None required\par
{\b Orientation:} Open end down (flat on the bed)\par
\par
{\b Fit Notes}\par
\par
The interior is sized with 0.3 mm per side clearance over the sensor body. If your printer runs tight, scale X/Y by 101\endash 102% or re-slice with slightly more horizontal expansion. If it\rquote s too loose, try 99%.\par
